    "problemStatement": "Chef has a simple undirected graph GGG with NNN vertices and MMM edges. A subgraph HHH of GGG is called good if:\n\n\nHHH is connected\nHHH contains all NNN vertices of GGG\nThere is a unique path between any two vertices in HHH, using only edges in HHH\nCount the number of good subgraphs of GGG. Since this number might be large, report it modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.\n\nIn other news, here's a completely unrelated image:\n\n.",
